Task: Add V2 migration, extend Order domain model (Green)

Summary: Added V2__add_reservation_to_orders.sql (reservation_id UUID NOT NULL,
reserved_quantity INT NOT NULL, status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'reserved'). Extended
Order with status/reservationId/reservedQuantity/createdAt (java.time.Instant — first
java.time usage in the codebase; circe 0.14's built-in Instant codec and Skunk's
timestamptz cover it).

Because extending Order's constructor forces every OrderStore implementation to supply
the new fields immediately, this commit necessarily also updates OrderStore.create's
signature (now takes reservationId/reservedQuantity) and adds OrderStore.get(id) for
both inMemory and postgres, plus OrderRoutes' POST handler to pass the reservation's
id/quantity through, and fixes the existing OrderStoreSuite/OrderStorePostgresSuite
call sites to compile. This gets most of Phase 2's implementation done ahead of
schedule — Phase 2 will still add dedicated new assertions (reservationId/status
round-tripping, get() returning None for unknown ids) since these fixes only kept
things compiling, they don't yet assert the new behavior.

